feat(mcp): open the tool surface from five to eight (#210)

The surface was closed in code, not merely by convention: Bind refused any
name outside the five, ToolNames() was asserted at length five in four test
files, and ratelimit.go refused to meter a sixth. That is what made a second
harness impossible to serve — not the idea, the registry.

describe_workspace, observe_tool_call and observe_session are added to
toolOrder and to the ADMIN side of #170's caller split, for the reason that
moved record_event there in #171: they are driven by the harness observing the
agent, never by the model reporting on itself. A model that could call
observe_tool_call could write its own activity log, which is doc 04 AB-14.

Names only. No implementation binds yet, so MissingTools() now reports the
three, and the start-up report and both health endpoints say so out loud —
ADR-0024's duty is what makes an incomplete surface safe rather than silent.
serve_test asserts exactly which three are outstanding, so each of #205, #206
and #207 fails here on the day it binds its tool, the same ratchet RM-068 left
for sign_commit.

Not pinned in protected-surfaces.sh: the gate reports mcp-tool 5 entries and
passes, proving it permits an addition. The three get pinned in #209, once a
second shim has driven them.

Driven by MCP-055, MCP-056 and MCP-057, observed failing on the undefined
names before any were declared. doc 01 §4 and §5 Phase 2 amended; doc 07
gains MCP-039..057 and OPS-019..023.

